        "original_id": "2cee1619-f2d6-5aff-aec2-aee39ee49fb0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ken Burns, Charles McDowell Jr., Mark Twain, Samuel Clemens, Sam R. Watkins\n- Works: Baseball, Tunisian Victory, The Congress, The Civil War, Mark Twain\n- Organizations: Public Broadcasting System\n- Events: North Africa Campaign\n- Topics: Documentary films, television miniseries, propaganda films, baseball\n\nFacts:\n- Tunisian Victory is a 1944 Anglo-American propaganda film about the victories in the North Africa Campaign.\n- Baseball is a 1994 American television documentary miniseries created by Ken Burns about the game of baseball.\n- Mark Twain is a documentary film on the life of Mark Twain, also known as Samuel Clemens, produced by Ken Burns in 2001.\n- Mark Twain aired on Public Broadcasting System on January 14 and 15, 2002.\n- Charles McDowell Jr. appeared in an interview in Ken Burns' documentary The Congress.\n- Charles McDowell Jr. provided the character voice for Sam R. Watkins in Ken Burns' documentary The Civil War.\n- Charles McDowell Jr. also provided a character voice and consultation for Ken Burns' documentary Baseball.",
